===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[evidence|Evidence]], particularly of a [[crime]], that is difficult or impossible to [[dispute]].
#: {{ux|en|We have a theory, but we haven't found a '''smoking gun''' yet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|title={{w|The Hacker Crackdown}}|isbn=0-553-56370-X|author=Bruce Sterling|authorlink=Bruce Sterling|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/101/101-h/101-h.htm|passage=When Prophet's place in Decatur, Georgia was raided in July 1989, there was the E911 Document, a '''smoking gun'''. And there was Prophet in the hands of the Secret Service, doing his best to "explain."}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=January 9, 2003|author=Hans Blix|authorlink=Hans Blix|work=UNMOVIC|title=Notes for Briefing the Security Council|url=https://www.un.org/depts/unmovic/recent%20items.html|passage=I now turn to the role and results of our current inspections. Evidently if we had found any ‘'''smoking gun'''’ we would have reported it to the Council.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michael Kinsley|date=June 12, 2005|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/opinions/2005/06/12/no-smoking-gun/584af460-0c4a-452c-bbb8-17f18fee163e/|title=No Smoking Gun|work=Washington Post|passage= It's all over the blogosphere and Air America, the left-wing talk radio network: This is the '''smoking gun''' of the Iraq war. It is proof positive that President Bush was determined to invade Iraq the year before he did so}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Peter Beaumont|title=Leading biologist dampens his ‘smoking gun’ Covid lab leak theory|work=The Guardian|date=2021-06-09|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/09/leading-biologist-dampens-his-smoking-gun-covid-lab-leak-theory|issn=0261-3077|passage=A Nobel prize-winning US biologist, who has been widely quoted describing a “'''smoking gun'''” to support the thesis that Covid-19 was genetically modified and escaped from a Wuhan lab, has said he overstated the case.}}

